Use `$md` when a template body should be formatted as Markdown.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    content = [$md:
        # Welcome

        This text becomes **formatted content**.
    ]
]

Small inline code spans use one backtick on each side.

Use `$code("moth")` or another language name for a full highlighted code block.

Moth Markdown stays small. It does not support fenced code
blocks or pipe tables.

### Automatic heading IDs

Static headings render kebab-case IDs from their visible labels, so a link can jump to a section.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    content = [$md:
        ## Getting started

        Jump back to @#getting-started (Getting started).
    ]
]

Advanced covers the full rules.
